      "title": "Melchizedek in the Argument",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "Hebrews reads the brief portrayal of Melchizedek alongside Psalm 110 as a literary analogy for Jesus\u2019 enduring priesthood. Thus the statements that Melchizedek is \u201cwithout father, without mother,\u201d and without an end of life describe how he functions in this textual argument; they do not require the conclusion that the Genesis figure literally lacked parents or was Jesus.",
          "verse_refs": [
